# Line-ending and binary policy for the repository.
#
# Why this file exists: without it, `format:check` gave a different answer on
# Windows and Linux. A Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` materialises
# CRLF in the working tree, Oxfmt normalises to LF, and so Oxfmt reported every
# text file as differing. On 2026-09-22 that accounted for roughly 97% of the
# ~8,850 reported differences; the genuine backlog against committed LF content
# was 219-284 tracked files. `format:check` cannot be a deterministic required
# gate until line endings are normalised here.
#
# Evidence: docs/audits/phase1-ci-integrity.md ("Format: the 8,800 differing
# files figure is mostly a checkout artifact").

# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository and in working trees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts must keep CRLF so they stay runnable when checked out
# on Windows.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.psm1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never apply line-ending conversion.
*.png          binary
*.jpg          binary
*.jpeg         binary
*.gif          binary
*.ico          binary
*.webp         binary
*.bmp          binary
*.pdf          binary
*.zip          binary
*.gz           binary
*.tgz          binary
*.tar          binary
*.bz2          binary
*.7z           binary
*.wasm         binary
*.node         binary
*.woff         binary
*.woff2        binary
*.ttf          binary
*.otf          binary
*.eot          binary
*.mp3          binary
*.mp4          binary
*.wav          binary
*.webm         binary
*.heapsnapshot binary
